# The processes' memory without extended memory (roadmap memory.md M4, E3):
# a 512 KB AT with none. The processes have what the boot modules left of
# the memory below 1 MB, so one of tests/posix/many.c's children of 60 KB
# fits, and the others are told there is no memory. Twelve children
# (TEST_MANY_FEWER), not 16, since the disk server (disk-scheduler.md M3)
# took the last 2-3 KB the sixteenth fork needed.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_MANY
define: TEST_MANY_FEWER
memory: 512K 0K
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
many: 12 children of 60 KB: forked 12, refused 0, sound 1, no memory 11, other 0
